    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.14), who both command elite status due to favorable platoon matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong park factor and a 4.28 xERA matchup against K. Montero, while **Luis Robert Jr.** is perfectly positioned against the southpaw M. P\u00e9rez. We are also leaning heavily on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), whose 19% boost from facing an aging and vulnerable Scherzer makes him a high-floor play despite the veteran's name value. While **Drake Baldwin** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are steady, the decision to start **Jacob Wilson** (62.19) atop the order against P. Tolle provides a necessary spark for our Roto categories, leveraging his 10% order bonus to maximize plate appearances.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Miguel Vargas** (51.80) on the bench. He posted a strong xwOBA of .390 and a solid score, but he narrowly missed the cut because the projected efficiency of our starting infield\u2014specifically the high-upside matchup for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2014created a ceiling we couldn't bypass. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** (58.25) remains in the lineup despite a slight dip due to the opposing pitcher's elite hold percentage; we need his speed in the mix to maintain our standing in the stolen base category. Managers should monitor the 31% rain risk affecting both **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Robert Jr.**; if these games are delayed or postponed, we will need to pivot to our depth, though we are currently comfortable riding out the weather forecast.",
